# Whole-struct per-element map as an OUTPUT — refused (Direction B)

The FUSION (PHASE5C-TUTORIAL §3a, 2026-08-25) inlines a whole-struct per-element
map — `map each g among source to (output of Callee with {…})` — ONLY when it
lands in an INTERNAL consumed per field: the struct list never exists on the
wire. The SAME shape declared as an OUTPUT is a `list of Callee` that must exist
on the wire (a caller could read the whole list), which has no clingo image — so
it stays refused, Direction B.

```catala
declaration scope Kamer:
  input grondslag content integer
  output bedrag content integer

scope Kamer:
  definition bedrag equals grondslag + 100

declaration scope Aanslag:
  input grondslagen content list of integer
  output shares content list of Kamer

scope Aanslag:
  definition shares equals
    map each g among grondslagen to
    (output of Kamer with { -- grondslag: g })
```
